  "summary": "I reconciled the medication lists for all four patients under RBC-TOC-02 and wrote a progress note for each. Five items are flagged to you: four messages and one task.\n\n**Walter Kim** (note doc-t0004)\n- **Furosemide:** changed to 40 mg twice daily (new order mr-t0001). The signed addendum (doc-00009) corrected the summary's 40 mg once daily, and the addendum rules.\n- **Potassium chloride:** stopped, as the summary says.\n- **Omeprazole:** kept. The pantoprazole on the discharge list was a hospital formulary substitute, so I did not order it.\n- **Unchanged:** metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin.\n- **FLAG – lisinopril is still on hold.** The 10/21 labs met the summary's condition for restarting it (creatinine 1.32, below 1.5). But potassium was 5.4, and the policy blocks restarting when it is above 5.0. I created task-t0003 for you, due 10/26, to review the repeat potassium.\n\n**Terence Stark** (note doc-t0008)\n- **Carvedilol:** raised to 12.5 mg twice daily (new order mr-t0005). The summary lists it as Coreg.\n- **Unchanged:** aspirin and insulin 70/30 at 18 units twice daily.\n- **FLAG – atorvastatin 80 mg not taken as prescribed:** his fills covered only about 24% of the 180 days before admission (last filled 03/04). I made no change; message comm-t0006.\n- **FLAG – glipizide 5 mg not mentioned in the discharge summary:** an outside endocrinologist prescribes it and he fills it regularly. There is no clinic order, so I did nothing; message comm-t0007. It's worth checking given he is also on insulin and has stage 3 kidney disease.\n\n**Adelaide Thompson** (note doc-t0012)\n- **Nifedipine ER:** raised to 60 mg daily (new order mr-t0009). The summary lists it as Procardia XL.\n- **Hydrochlorothiazide:** stopped. The signed addendum says stop and do not restart because it caused her low sodium, which overrides the summary's \"continue\".\n- **FLAG – levothyroxine 100 mcg not taken as prescribed:** fills covered only about 41% of the 180 days before admission, and her hospital TSH was 7.9. I made no change; message comm-t0011.\n\n**Earnest Roberts** (note doc-t0015)\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg:** restarted from hold. The 10/22 outside lab report showed creatinine 1.08, meeting the summary's condition of below 1.3. Potassium was 4.6 on that report, under the 5.0 limit; his 10/20 clinic value had been 5.3.\n- **Rosuvastatin:** kept. The atorvastatin on the discharge list was a hospital formulary substitute, so I did not order it.\n- **Unchanged:** insulin glargine and insulin lispro.\n- **FLAG – sertraline 100 mg not mentioned in the discharge summary:** an outside psychiatrist prescribes it and there is no clinic order, so I did nothing; message comm-t0014.\n\nFor all four, the pharmacy fill histories showed no other gaps or unaddressed medications.",
